---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, url } from "../site";
const updated = "November 9, 2026";
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="What data Data Science Chronicles collects, why, and how to opt out." path="/privacy/">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Last updated {updated}.</p></header>
    <div class="prose page-body">
      <p>This blog ({SITE.origin}{SITE.base}/) is run by {SITE.author}. It has no accounts and doesn't ask you for personal information.</p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        I use Google Analytics 4 to understand which articles are read and how people find them. It uses cookies and
        collects things like pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser, and clicks on outbound and affiliate
        links. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site may use Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies to serve ads based on your visits to this and
        other websites. You can turn off personalised ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>
        or opt out of third-party vendors at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some links go to partners such as Amazon or course providers. When you click them, those sites may set cookies to
        attribute a purchase. See the <a href={url("/disclosure/")}>affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Comments</h2>
      <p>Comments use Giscus (GitHub Discussions) and load only when you scroll to them. Posting requires a GitHub account and is covered by GitHub's privacy statement.</p>
      <h2>Your preferences</h2>
      <p>The light/dark theme choice is stored in your browser's local storage and never sent anywhere.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.socials.email}`}>{SITE.socials.email}</a> with any privacy request.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
